  "notes": "Modified cash basis village, FY ended 2024-09-30. Governmental beginning/ending are the governmental funds fund balances (p4: 480,643 -> 349,028), which include cash, CDs, restricted cash and a 360 receivable net of 2,944 payroll withholdings. Transfers: governmental total column prints only Net interfund transfers in (out) (4,215), recorded as transfers_out 4,215; the utilities receive net 4,215 (p6). The Taxes line 82,369 is the Statement of Activities' Property tax 82,369 (p2). Intergovernmental 218,629 and Grants and donations 193,412 are kept as printed (broad groups); the Statement of Activities general receipts show their make-up. Business-type measure is net position (modified cash); no single receipts total printed, so receipts total computed; disbursements 199,307 = Utilities disbursements on p2 (operating 92,138 + loan payments 100,999 + capital purchases 6,170). Roll-forward 626,067 + 224,878 - 199,307 + 4,215 = 655,853. Detail: the Budgetary Comparison Schedule (p7, report p17) is a combined all-funds schedule with a single 'Receipts and transfers' line, so per user rule 2026-10-27 detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds (p4) and business-type (p6) statements. Balance sheet (user rule 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds Balance Sheet (p3), whose totals equal the government-wide governmental column (p1); business-type lines and totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Read pages 1-7 of 7"
}
